i've always assumed that interested parties were recording what they
considered to be interesting ideas. the dev team does the work and i think
that they should be free to do that work as they please. if they want to
become beholden to the net then that's their business but i don't see
where that's necessary. working in their own way they've managed to make
the game appealing to a wide audience.

for those that can write the code, the way to introduce changes is to make
patches and deliver them to the dev team (nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu).
include liberal comments and reasoning, etc. for the rest of us (not doing
the work) the hope is that perhaps an interesting idea will catch a coders
attention. i can't make a reasonable argument for the coders to do our
bidding based on popular opinion since we aren't supporting them ...

